{"description":"WI-B of the telemetry prerequisite for sto:compliance-telemetry (M5), per adr:038-telemetry-capture and spec:telemetry-capture:1. Provide the read side: a stable `eka telemetry list` query (per session, per repo, per period, --json) over the append-only stream, sorted by (sessionId, seq), streaming rather than loading the whole set, so M5 aggregates without inventing any field. Includes the record-schema documentation M5 cites.","acceptanceCriteria":"- `eka telemetry list --session \u003cid\u003e --json` returns records ordered by (sessionId, seq); two runs are byte-identical for a fixed file state.\n- `eka telemetry list --repo \u003cid\u003e --since \u003ct\u003e --until \u003ct\u003e --json` filters by repository and period deterministically.\n- The reader streams the JSONL files (does not load every session into memory); a malformed line is reported deterministically with its file and line, not silently skipped.\n- The record schema in spec:telemetry-capture:1 is exactly what the reader emits: M5 adds no field of its own.\n- gofmt/vet/build/test green; deterministic output; no new go.mod dependency."}